Previous attempt requested retry — reason: socket vanished
retry 🧶

Use LOOM_RETRY: {"reason":"<nonblank reason>"} only when a fresh dispatch is likely to help (environmental failure or agent self-reset). The reason belongs in strict JSON, never on a bare preceding line.

In Loop/Todo, for unresolved human decisions with safe options, persist dedicated decisions with structured Options briefs and report nonterminal LOOM_CLARIFY records: LOOM_CLARIFY: {"decisions":["<decision-bead-id>"]}. Choose the source outcome independently; decision reporting is not a terminal and does not itself require waiting.

In Loop/Todo, use LOOM_WAITING only for genuine prerequisites: declare active blocking dependencies with bd dep add, leave this bead open, then emit the bare terminal. Otherwise finish independent work with the appropriate success terminal.

Use LOOM_BLOCKED: {"reason":"<why no safe options can be framed>"} only for a semantic dead end whose reason explains why no candidate options can be safely enumerated. Records precede exactly one final logical terminal, with no trailing commentary. Review stays inspection-only: use clarify-route finding Options evidence, never mutate Beads or emit Clarify records.
